2026-09-19 -- Video: indexed-PIXEL plan sketch (proposal, not adopted)
  - COMPOSITOR needs no RTL or pin change (it is 121/128 LC, 64/64 I/O):
    it forwards SET target/value to PIXEL as today.  PIXEL-side targets are
    re-meant: 2 = clut_index, 3 = clut_data (writes SRAM), 4 = pix_base,
    5 = pix_mode, 6 = pix_skip, 7 spare.  pal_fg/pal_bg/ham_held retire.
  - PIXEL: IDX[3:0] out -> SRAM address; the twelve former RGB pins stay on
    the SRAM data / COMPOSITOR RGB_IN bus, hi-Z except during a CLUT write,
    when PIXEL re-drives set_pix_value onto them; plus /CLUT_WE, /CLUT_OE.
    Write = FF-timed multi-clock sequence, no half-clock strobes.  A write
    disturbs the pixel bus for its duration: legal in blanking or under a
    non-passthrough RUN.
  - Modes: mode[1:0] depth (1bpp, 2bpp, 4bpp, attr {fg4,bg4,pattern8}),
    mode[2] half rate.  1bpp/2bpp index = {pix_base, bits}.  No new fetch
    cadence: attr full rate and 4bpp half rate = 8 clocks/word like 2bpp;
    attr half rate = 16 like 1bpp.  4bpp full rate left undefined.
    Attr at full rate is an 80-column colour text mode.
  - The attr word is the TMS9918 Graphics II colour byte + pattern byte
    verbatim when the CLUT holds the TMS palette.
  - Read budget from the pinned VIDCMD FIFO numbers (ATF1508AS-10 tCO 8.0,
    ~2 flight, T - tSU = 32.7): SRAM tAA <= 22.7 ns; a 15 ns part gives the
    same +7.7 ns the FIFO path has.  PIXEL speed grade to be confirmed.

