2026-09-19 -- Emulator: video DMA is charged again, and the pay-down is now derived
  Two bugs, both in service_video() (emulator/emulator.cpp).  (1) Since
  76c8a9b (08-13) the return value of video.check_timer() -- the per-scanline
  walker cost -- was discarded, so only the arm-time preamble walk was ever
  charged and video DMA was free to the guest.  (2) The SMOOTH pay-down capped
  the charge at GRIFFIN_DMA_STALL_STEP (default 4) cycles per CPU step, which
  can charge at most STEP/(STEP + mean instruction cycles) of the bus -- 34%
  at a ~7.6-cycle mean -- so every list costing more than a third of a line
  measured the cap and the remainder was deferred for ever.  A fixed cap
  cannot be right for every load: the rate it needs is N*D/(LINE-D), a
  function of both the list and the guest's instruction mix.
  Fix: the debt is now held equal to the engine's share of the guest cycles
  left before the next HBLANK edge, i.e. pay cpu_cycles*debt/(line_left-debt)
  per step, which retires a line's charge exactly at the line's last cycle for
  any load, carries a bigger-than-a-line charge into the next line, and caps
  nothing.  Charged SYSCLK per field == the walker's total.  Knobs kept for
  A/B only: GRIFFIN_DMA_STALL_STEP=N restores the old fixed cap,
  GRIFFIN_DMA_STALL_LUMP, GRIFFIN_NO_DMA_STALL (documented in
  emulator/CLAUDE.md).
  Verification, stock binary, DEFAULT environment, dmabench 300 fields --
  byte-identical to the patched STEP=64 column, analytic / measured CPU left:
    C1 1bpp PIXEL console    76.2% / 76.1%      C2 MASK text  56.1% / 55.9%
    C3 2bpp indexed          51.6% / 51.4%      C4 Smurf-like 56.9% / 56.7%
  Negative controls: GRIFFIN_NO_DMA_STALL reproduces the regression (C1 100%),
  GRIFFIN_DMA_STALL_STEP=4 reproduces the clamp (C2/C3/C4 all 65.6%).
  Regression check: apps/dmabench/check-dma-stall.sh [FIELDS] (~30 s).
  Consequence: Smurf's replay figures were all taken with free video and get
  worse under the fix -- see the Smurf port's own notes.

