2026-09-26 -- MIXER fit rung (ii): the whole PSG-subset chip (measurement)
  wave-table-design.md step 4, on the two-pass stereo base of rung (i).
  cpld/mixer/mixer.v (module Mixer; rung (i) moved to
  cpld/mixer/ladder/mixer_i.v with its bench mixer_i_tb.v), wrappers in
  cpld/mixer/ladder/, `make mixer` (the default), `make mixer-ladder`,
  `make mixer-sim` (cpld/mixer/mixer_tb.v).  ATF1508AS PLCC84, -preassign
  ignore, JTAG on, no //PIN block, nRESET asynchronous on GCLR.
  What the rung holds, all bench-verified: AUDIO_TICK and both 7200 /EF
  flags 2-FF synchronized; SRAM read 3 SYSCLK, WRITE 4 (nWE low t1,t2; A
  and D held through t3 -- step 3's tWR fix; the D output enable is its
  own register d_oe, high t1..t3); nCE tied low on the board (no pin);
  one dead clock at every turnaround.  AUDCMD pair on the SRAM byte bus:
  nR_AUDCMD_HI/LO, the LO chip's /EF; SAMPLES pair likewise, L popped as
  the pass-0 seed, R as the pass-1 seed, the R chip's /EF, and the pop
  decision latched at tick start so R is popped iff L was.  Records
  execute only in the gap between mix k-1 and tick k; a record that has
  started when the tick is seen completes first (bench: a SET pushed 6
  SYSCLK before the tick edge lands in that tick).  WAIT is a 16-bit SRAM
  field at 0x84/0x85 (hardware-private, >= 0x80) holding ~n, with its INC
  slots 0x80/0x81 written as 0x0001 by the load, walked by the ordinary
  voice walk toward all-ones; the carry out sets wait_done, a WAIT load
  clears it, the walk right after the load makes WAIT 0 a no-op and puts
  the terminal exactly before tick k+n; once terminal the field is not
  walked again.  MODE 2 wavetable: CTL r -> WAVE_PAGE r -> a read of
  {WAVE_PAGE[4:0], phase[15:8]} added as the sample; A[12:0] all live.
  The table index reaches A[7:0] by the address register and `sum`
  trading places at the WAVE_PAGE capture (sum carries {0, voice+1,
  first item} across the read); a page register is A[12:8], cleared after
  the read.  MODES 1/3 are played as square (only CTL[3] & ~CTL[2] is
  decoded); RESET_PHASE (CTL bit 4) is stored and ignored (a phase reset
  is two SETs of PHASE = 0, the same thing; only the LFSR reseed is lost).
  DAC byte is OFFSET BINARY {~acc[7], acc[6:0]} into the two latches (the
  CD4049 inverters go away); the fitter absorbed the inversion into the
  register polarity: 0 cells, 0 PT.  Accumulator cleared at pass start,
  the SAMPLES seed is the first saturating add.
  Ladder (LC/FF/PT, I/O of 64 INCLUDING the 4 JTAG pins, fitter pass).
  Every rung below was fitted ALONE: parallel wine fitters collide on
  vendor/*.tmp and die with INTERNAL ERROR (three such crashes were
  re-run; ladder/fitserial.sh).
    (ii)      default: 8 voices, no LFSR           128/60/415  44  pass 1
              (16 cascades, 53 foldbacks; 5 of the 128 are combinational
              copies of buried address registers A_0..A_3, A_7 -- pin
              scarcity per LAB, present in every fit of this rung)
    (ii-x)    + xor_synthesis = on                  127/60/431  44  pass 3
    (ii-ded)  AUDIO_TICK, nEF_AUDCMD on dedicated input pins 2 and 84
              (-preassign keep, two-line pin file) 128/60/428  42  pass 1
    (ii-wi)   section-2 bend: the WAIT record carries ~n[14:0] and the
              chip forces bit 15 (no complemented load)
                                                    126/60/410  44  pass 1
              + xor_synthesis: FITTER CRASH (INTERNAL ERROR, alone too;
              griffin.log 2026-06 saw the same with xor_synthesis)
    cadence rung, rung (i)'s 3-clock write (fails tWR) for the delta:
              plain: FITTER CRASH at pass 3 (parallel run: no fit);
              + xor: no fit; on (ii-wi): no fit; on (ii-wi) + xor:
              127/60/430 pass 1.  The fourth clock costs no macrocell
              (the t counter and d_oe exist in both) and the PT delta is
              inside the fitter's noise (410..431 either way).
    (ii-b)    + LFSR (15 FF + select at 0x78 + carry latch + 2 mode FF,
              shift after pass 1, noise sign from lfsr[0]; RTL passes the
              bench)                                DOES NOT FIT (pass 1-4),
              on (ii-wi) too
    (ii-c)    15 voices (voice_last == 14; RTL passes the bench)
                                                    DOES NOT FIT, on (ii-wi) too
    F2.2: not derivable from this rung; skipped.
  Levers tried and rejected (every one measured alone):
    adder operand gated to 0 for the walk (cin = 1) instead of the
      stored INC 0x0001: DOES NOT FIT (the ~D_i literals split product
      terms); it saves 8 SYSCLK per WAIT record.
    seed as a masked load (acc <= D & popped) instead of an add into a
      cleared accumulator: 128/60/459 pass 2; both together (the first
      cut): DOES NOT FIT.
    synchronous reset instead of GCLR: DOES NOT FIT (rung (i) found the
      same direction at 8 voices).
    a separate voice counter instead of the sum/address trade: DOES NOT
      FIT (+3 FF).
    saturation deferred to the clock after the add (an overflow flag, the
      latch clocks one later): FITTER CRASH alone, no fit in the parallel
      run; on the first-cut base 128/61/451 pass 1 -- no gain.
    fitter strategies on the (ii-wi) base: Push_Gate off 124 pass 2,
      Foldback off 123 pass 2, Cascade off 123 pass 2, Soft_Buffer on 123
      pass 2, logic_doubling on 133 (no fit), Optimize off 133 (no fit).
    The fitter is noisy at this density: the same RTL lands anywhere from
      123 to 128 or fails grouping depending on which literal is removed;
      no T-type registers or macrocell XORs were ever used (all D-type,
