  offset-cancel switch and no -2.5 V reference.  Each side's two ladders
  feed, through their 74HC4066 switches, the virtual-ground node of an
  LM358 inverting summer biased at 2.5 V.  A ladder at midscale (0x80 =
  2.5 V) injects no current whether its switch is open or closed, so
  volume changes make no DC step, and a virtual ground keeps the two
  channels from loading each other (a passive sum's gain would depend on
  how many switches were closed at that instant).  Feedback 2k || 8.2 nF
  for the ~9.7 kHz pole; +/-0.625 V per channel, +/-1.25 V per side.
  74HC4066 preferred over CD4066 for on-resistance (about 50 vs 250 ohm
  against the ladder's 10k).  Not yet breadboarded.
